==Overview==
<tabber>
Pros=
{{Overview|Pros
|'''General'''
* High damage.
* Good for use at close range.
* Good stuns and mobility.
* Great combo potential.
* Both moves can target multiple enemies at the same time.
* Relatively easy to obtain at any level above 1250.
* Both moves can hit [[Sea Beast]]s.
* No M1 dash, making it a great choice for grinding.

|'''[Z] Portal Opening'''
* Decent hitbox.
* Can be triggered without [[Instinct/Break|breaking Instinct]].
* Decent knockback (depends on angle).

|'''[X] Cresent Dash'''
* Decent for mobility.
}}

|-|Cons=
{{Overview|Cons
|'''General'''
* Cannot damage [[Blade]] users.
* Small hitbox.
* Short range.
* Moves are hard to use with [[Buddha]]
* Vulnerable to attacks when casting a move.
* Both moves are easily escapable with [[Instinct]].

|'''[Z] Portal Opening'''
* Cannot be triggered without an enemy.
* Does not true-stun, meaning it can countered during the move's animation if Instinct-tricked.
* High knockback makes it difficult to grind with unless used as a finisher.

|'''[X] Cresent Dash'''
* Dash is quite slow and can be dodged easily.
}}
</tabber>

==Trivia==
* The old version of the Midnight Blade is used by the Lv. 1325 [[Raid Bosses|Raid Boss]], [[Cursed Captain]].
* The afterimage caused by the [Z] move holds an unreleased redesign.
* When reached 100 [[Ectoplasm]], the [[Titles|title:]] "The Ghost" #152 will be obtained.
* Midnight Blades reworked model is one of the most controversial redesigns of a sword in-game, as its old design had much more detail and looked cleaner.

